 "info": {
  "description": "Bounded simulator subset of the official Amazon Keyspaces API (2022-02-10). Every other official operation returns HTTP 501 UnknownOperationException. Keyspaces, tables and user-defined types are stored configuration records: no Cassandra data plane, CQL endpoint, row, partition or capacity exists, tables are ACTIVE at once, and RestoreTable, GetTableAutoScalingSettings, UpdateKeyspace and UntagResource return UnknownOperationException with HTTP 501. The AWS-owned system keyspaces are not listed, and creating a keyspace with one of their names (system, system_schema, system_schema_mcs, system_multiregion_info) fails with ConflictException. Only single-Region keyspaces exist: replicationSpecification must be SINGLE_REGION (the default) without a regionList, so UpdateKeyspace, which can only add a Region, is not implemented, replicaSpecifications are refused and no replication status is reported. CreateTable and UpdateTable refuse cdcSpecification and replicaSpecifications; autoScalingSpecification and addColumns are refused because their effects cannot be stored, so a table schema cannot change after creation. UntagResource is not implemented because it takes key and value pairs and the catalog removes tags by key. Table schemas must name at least one partition key, define every column once (names compare case-insensitively), list partition, clustering and static columns among the columns without reusing a column as both a key and a static column, and use CQL types: the scalar types of the Keyspaces data type list, or list, set, map, tuple and frozen collections of them with user-defined types only inside frozen; user-defined type names are not resolved. Capacity defaults to PAY_PER_REQUEST and PROVISIONED needs readCapacityUnits and writeCapacityUnits, a customer managed key needs kmsKeyIdentifier (stored without contacting KMS), and encryption defaults to AWS_OWNED_KMS_KEY and point-in-time recovery to DISABLED; no earliest restorable time, streams or table size are reported. User-defined type names are 1 to 48 letters, digits and underscores starting with a letter and are stored in lowercase as documented (double-quoted names are refused); fields need distinct names and CQL types, references between types are not resolved, so directReferringTables and directParentTypes stay empty and maxNestingDepth is not reported. Keyspace and table names are stored as given, are unique per Region and keyspace, and a keyspace deletes its tables and types with it. Resource counts (50 keyspaces per Region, 50 tables and 50 types per keyspace) are local limits. Operations are authorized as the Keyspaces IAM actions cassandra:Create, Select, Alter, Drop and TagResource on the keyspace, table or type ARN (arn:aws:cassandra:region:account:/keyspace/name/table/name), without the additional Select on the system keyspace that AWS requires for the read operations. ListTagsForResource refuses nextToken and maxResults and returns all tags.",
  "title": "Amazon Keyspaces (for Apache Cassandra) (simulator catalog)",
  "version": "2022-02-10"
 },
